# A fresh brief says it has nothing, names its source choices, and a refresh
# fills the page with the live list. Assertions stay on stable text: the
# fetch stamp, the source name, the offline line and the pager, never a story
# title.
wait-for Daily brief
expect Nothing yet
expect refreshes itself each morning
expect not fetched yet
clean
shot brief-empty
tap Source
wait-for All four are public Hacker News lists
expect What held up over several days
clean
shot brief-sources
tap-id source-best
wait-for Best
tap Brief
wait-for Daily brief
expect Best
tap Refresh
wait-for as of
expect Best of the week
# The time is said as the reader's own ("as of today, 22:12"), and the stories
# behind the headlines are being kept for reading offline. A check for "UTC"
# missing matched live headlines such as "Dutch", so the route looks for the
# spoken time instead.
expect as of today,
expect eady offline
expect 1 of
clean
shot brief-stories
tap-id next
wait-for 2 of
tap-id previous
wait-for 1 of
